# The Icepi Zero's netlist equals the RTL for all time. From all flops 0, for every input
# sequence on the pins, the pads' inputs, the PLL's outputs and the three macro cores'
# outputs, uo and the inputs of the pads, the PLL and the cores agree every cycle;
# configured.awk's miter from the configured state too. Synthesis before place and route:
# synth_ecp5's JSON, which nextpnr-ecp5 places as it stands. The Makefile checks each
# miter's first cycle by BMC and every later one from each state the first reaches
# (tempor), with ABC scorr + dprove, which match flops by function, not name.
#
# Trusted: yosys's frontend, proc, flatten and memory_map; yosys's models of the ECP5
# cells (lattice/common_sim.vh, ccu2c_sim.vh) and DP16KD.v's of the block RAM as the
# macro core, which nextpnr-ecp5, ecppack and the silicon have to agree with; the pads,
# the PLL and the cores as shared cut points, the cores from the same contents (INITVAL's
# 0 on the board), and cells_io.vh's mapping of icepi_top's pads; one rising-edge clock
# but Both_edges' falling pair, stepping with it (asserted in gold.ys and gate.ys); an
# asynchronous reset acting in the cycle it is asserted, on both sides; timing, which is
# nextpnr's. Each flop of a recoded state machine matches the RTL's binary state compared
# with one value, as in netlist_equiv/miter.ys. The x's the cell models leave on the
# address and data of a distributed RAM write not enabled become free inputs, as does
# DP16KD.v's port A in a mode it does not model: the proof holds for every value.
# Teeth: make icepi_equiv_teeth.

read_rtlil gold.il
read_rtlil gate.il
miter -equiv -flatten gold gate miter
hierarchy -top miter
delete t:$scopeinfo
# for configured.awk
write_rtlil miter_pre.il
script ../netlist_equiv/aig.ys
write_aiger miter.aig
